# Narrator: the Village of Barovia (docs/voice/narrator.md). Second person, present tense, one or two sentences.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Locations

~ enter:village_of_barovia
| The village sits in the valley like something left out in the rain: grey roofs, nailed shutters, mud to the ankle. Smoke rises from a few chimneys, and from none of them in a hurry.
| [flag.death_house_completed and not flag.burgomaster_buried] Out of the house, into the open air, which turns out to be only slightly larger. Behind every shutter, someone is pretending not to watch you.
| [flag.burgomaster_buried] The village looks the same as it did, which is to say exhausted. A few more shutters stand open a finger's width than before.
| [flag.ireena_in_party] Doors open a crack as Ireena passes and close again, and nobody calls out to her. A few people touch their foreheads, as if at a funeral.
cooldown 30

~ enter:blood_of_the_vine
| Smoke, sour wine, and the low talk of people who have learned to talk low. Every head turns when the door opens, and then, one by one, turns back.
| [flag.ismark_met] The tavern is as you left it. The hearth table is empty without Ismark at it; the wine is no better without him.
cooldown 20

~ enter:burgomaster_mansion
| Every window is boarded from inside, and the boards are scored with claw marks on the outside of the wood. The house smells of candle wax, wet dog and grief.
| [flag.burial_procession] The house is emptier without the coffin in it. Somehow the boards on the windows look less sure of themselves.
| [flag.mansion_siege_survived] Splintered boards, fresh nails, a long scorch on the hall floor: the house held. It looks surprised about it.
cooldown 20

~ enter:village_church
| Cold candles, cracked windows and a sunburst over the altar gone grey with soot. Under your boots, faint through the floorboards, someone is weeping and someone is praying, and you can't tell which is which.
| [flag.doru_destroyed] The church is quiet now, and the candles are lit. Someone has swept the floor, badly, as if with shaking hands.
| [flag.doru_freed] The church is quiet now, and the undercroft door stands open. The quiet is worse than the screaming was; screaming, at least, stayed in one place.
cooldown 20

~ enter:bildraths_mercantile
| A bell rings as the door opens, and somewhere a pencil starts moving. Every shelf is dusted, every label straight, every price outrageous.
| [flag.bildrath_robbed] The bell rings. The pencil stops.
cooldown 20

~ enter:mad_marys_house
| Three locks on the door, boards on every window, and a cold stove in the middle of it all. The weeping fills the house the way water fills a jar.
| [flag.gertruda_search_promised and not flag.gertruda_home] The weeping is quieter than it was. Mary is mending something by the stove, and keeps glancing at the door.
| [flag.gertruda_home] The boards are off one window. Two cups by the stove, and somebody humming in the back room.
cooldown 20

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Village areas

~ enter:mansion_yard
| A yard of dead hedges and churned mud inside an iron fence. The mud holds paw prints the size of dinner plates, all of them pointed at the house.
once

~ enter:north_lane
| Boarded houses lean together along the lane like mourners at a graveside. Through a gap in one shutter, an eye watches you go by, and blinks.
once

~ enter:churchyard
| Old graves lean in the long grass, and the church watches them from its rise like a tired shepherd. The lych-gate creaks shut behind you on its own.
| [flag.burial_procession and not flag.burgomaster_buried] The coffin waits on its trestles beside the fresh grave. Ireena stands at the head of it, very straight, as if guarding the door of a house.
| [flag.burgomaster_buried] The burgomaster's grave is the only neat thing in the churchyard. Somebody has already left a candle on it.
cooldown 10

~ enter:village_road_west
| The road west runs out between the last houses, toward the crossroads. High to the south-west, on a cliff of black rock, a castle sits against the clouds and does not need to be introduced.
once

~ enter:village_square
| A square of mud around a dry well. Two shops face it, one tavern and one mercantile, and both look as if they're waiting for customers who stopped coming years ago.
| [not flag.burgomaster_buried and not flag.morgantha_driven_off] A square of mud around a dry well, and in the middle of it all a pastry cart, the only cheerful thing in the village. That should worry you more than it does.
| [flag.burgomaster_buried] The square is empty. The pastry cart has gone, leaving two wheel ruts that lead out of the village toward the west.
cooldown 15

~ enter:village_road_east
| The road east runs back the way you came, toward the gates and the mist beyond them. The mist has not moved; it doesn't need to.
once

~ enter:mary_lane
| Somewhere down the lane, a woman is weeping: not loudly, but without stopping, the way rain falls in a place where it always rains.
| [flag.gertruda_search_promised] The weeping from the shuttered house has softened to something nearer to humming. It is not a happy tune.
cooldown 15

~ enter:mercantile_front
| A lantern burns over the mercantile door, the only lamp lit on the street. Bildrath, you suspect, is billing someone for it.
once

~ enter:back_lanes
| The back lanes are narrow, muddy and full of collapsed fences. A cat watches you from a rain barrel with the calm of something that has outlived several owners.
once

~ enter:death_house_lot
| A tall, handsome house behind a rusted fence, its windows dark, its porch swept. It is the best-kept house in the village, and nobody will walk past it.
| [flag.death_house_refused] Bricks fill the doorway where the front door used to be, and the tall window you came out of is half bricked over already. The house is mending itself, slowly, like a scab.
| [flag.death_house_sacrificed] The house is quiet. It has the stillness of something that has been fed and is in no hurry for its next meal.
| [flag.death_house_children_at_rest] The house is only a house now, and the road at the village edge is only a road.
cooldown 15

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Interior areas

~ enter:tavern_common_room
| Low beams, a smoking hearth, a dozen tables and four drinkers. At the corner table, three women in bright skirts are laughing, which in this village is practically a crime.
once

~ enter:tavern_bar
| Behind the bar the casks are stacked three high, and when Arik taps the top one it rings hollow. Only one of them still sloshes.
once

~ enter:tavern_back_room
| A storeroom of empty crates and dust. On a crate in the corner sits a leather satchel nobody has touched in weeks, tidily, as if waiting for its owner to come back for it.
once

~ enter:mansion_hall
| A hall of portraits and boarded windows, a staircase climbing into the dark. Somebody has nailed a plank across the front door from inside, and another, and another.
once

~ enter:mansion_study
| A burgomaster's study: ledgers, maps of the valley, a desk buried in papers. On top of the pile, one letter is written in a hand that grows shakier toward the end.
once

~ enter:mansion_kitchen
| A kitchen that has been feeding three people on rations for a month. A cleaver lies on the table, not for cooking.
once

~ enter:mansion_parlor
| A small fire, a worn settee, a sword leaning against the hearth within easy reach. Whoever sits in this room has been sitting up nights.
once

~ enter:mansion_wake_room
| The coffin rests on trestles between two new candles. Someone replaces them every few hours, and doesn't sleep in between.
| [flag.burial_procession] Two burned-out candles and two empty trestles. The room still feels like it's holding its breath.
cooldown 30

~ enter:church_nave
| Rows of empty pews face an altar under a grey sunburst. The floor is cold enough to feel through your boots, and it isn't only cold that comes up through it.
once

~ enter:church_altar
| The altar is scrubbed bare. Wax has run down its sides in long pale ropes, from candles that burned all night, every night, for a long time.
once

~ enter:church_vestry
| A cupboard of a room with vestments on pegs and a chest under the window. Everything here has been folded with great care by someone whose hands were shaking.
once

~ enter:undercroft_stairwell
| The stair turns down into the dark. The bar has left fresh gouges in its brackets, and the bottom edge of the door is scored with marks like fingernails, from the other side.
once

~ enter:undercroft
| The undercroft smells of old stone, old bones and something fresher. The dark here is very thick, and very attentive.
| [flag.doru_destroyed] Empty niches, cold stone, and a heap of rags in the corner. Whatever lived here doesn't any longer, in either sense.
| [flag.doru_freed] The undercroft is empty. On the ceiling, the scratches lead to the stair and up it, and stop.
cooldown 20

~ enter:mercantile_shop
| A shop so tidy it feels like a reprimand. Behind the counter, each shelf is labeled, and each label has a price, and each price has been written in ink so it can't be argued with.
once

~ enter:mercantile_storeroom
| Crates, sacks, barrels and, in the far corner, a small iron strongbox that sits on the floor like a toad.
once

~ enter:mary_front_room
| A rocking chair by a cold stove, a sewing basket, a girl's dress folded neatly over the arm of the chair. Someone has set two places at the table and eaten from neither.
once

~ enter:gertruda_room
| A narrow bed, a chest, a shelf of children's books and a window with its shutter hanging open. The room is very clean, and nothing in it has been moved since she left.
once

~ enter:mary_bedroom
| A bed that hasn't been slept in, and a chair pulled up to the wall that adjoins her daughter's room. The plaster is worn smooth at the height of an ear.
once

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Village props

~ examine:village_well
| The well is dry, the rope still tied, the bucket somewhere down in the dark. Someone has carved a sunburst into the lip, and someone else has tried to scrape it off.
cooldown 10

~ examine:well_rope
| A well rope, tied tighter than a well rope needs to be. It's taut, as if something heavier than a bucket is hanging at the other end.
cooldown 10

~ search:well_rope
| Hand over hand, the rope brings up a waxed pouch knotted to the bucket: somebody's escape money, or somebody's escape potion, left for a night that never came.

~ examine:village_notice
| A notice board, every notice on it the same notice: curfew, by order of the burgomaster. The newest copy is three weeks old, and someone has added a line underneath.
cooldown 10

~ examine:castle_glimpse
| Castle Ravenloft stands on its pillar of rock above the valley, its towers lost in cloud. One window high up is lit, as it always is.
| [class:wizard] Castle Ravenloft, above the valley, with one high window lit. {name} would wager a good book that the room behind it is full of them.
cooldown 10

~ examine:road_west_gates
| The road west, out of the village toward the crossroads. The mud is printed with wolf tracks going both ways, and boot prints going one.
cooldown 10

~ examine:road_east_mists
| The road east runs back toward the gates, and the mist lies across it like a held breath. Nobody has come in from that direction in a long time, except you.
cooldown 10

~ examine:mansion_front_door
| The door is oak, iron-bound and scored to splinters around the latch. Somebody has nailed a horseshoe over it upside down, and somebody else, or something, has bent it.
cooldown 10

~ examine:mansion_claw_marks
| Long parallel gouges climb the walls of the mansion as high as the upstairs sills. Whatever made them could stand on its hind legs and reach the windows.
| [class:fighter] Claw marks, five deep, at the height of a man's throat, made by something with a reach {name} would rather not meet in a doorway.
cooldown 10

~ examine:boarded_houses
| Every door on the lane is boarded over from inside, which means the people who live here nailed themselves in. Behind the boards, a child's voice asks a question and is hushed.
cooldown 10

~ examine:abandoned_handcart
| A handcart tipped over in the lane, one wheel missing, its load gone. A child's shoe lies in the mud beside it; the other is nowhere.
cooldown 10

~ examine:church_facade
| The church stands on its rise with its bell tower leaning slightly toward the castle, as if listening. Half its windows are boarded; the other half are dark.
cooldown 10

~ examine:old_graves
| Old headstones, their names worn to dimples. Several have been dug around recently, as if the earth was checking on them.
cooldown 10

~ examine:open_grave
| A fresh grave beside a headstone that reads only "Beloved". The earth is piled neatly, ready to go back in.
| [flag.parriwimple_pallbearer] A fresh grave, very deep and very square, its spoil heap so tidy it looks measured. It was.
cooldown 10

~ examine:kolyan_grave
| Kolyan Indirovich, burgomaster, beside his wife. The earth is fresh and the candle on it is still burning, though nobody has been seen to light it.
| [flag.burial_method == "hasty"] A rough mound of earth, no marker yet, no candle. The burgomaster's grave looks like what it was: a hurry.
cooldown 10

~ examine:tavern_sign
| A painted sign of a bunch of grapes dripping red into a cup: the Blood of the Vine. The paint has run in the damp, so the cup looks rather fuller than intended.
cooldown 10

~ examine:price_board
| A board of prices in neat black letters, each number roughly ten times what it should be. Underneath, smaller: "Browsing: free, for now."
cooldown 10

~ examine:mary_window
| A shuttered window with a candle burning behind the slats. The weeping comes from just inside, and it doesn't stop when you stop to listen.
cooldown 10

~ examine:morgantha_cart
| A handcart heaped with glazed pastries under a white cloth. They smell of honey and warm butter and something else, faint and sleepy, underneath.
| [species:halfling] Pastries, golden and glistening: {name}'s stomach makes a case for them, and {name}'s instincts make a better one against.
cooldown 10

~ examine:collapsed_barn
| A barn that gave up some winter ago and lay down where it stood. Something has been sleeping under the fallen roof: the straw is pressed flat in a circle the size of a cart.
cooldown 10

~ examine:death_house_facade
| A handsome townhouse, freshly painted, its windows dark. It has the look of a house expecting guests, and looking forward to them.
| [flag.death_house_refused] The front door is bricked up, and so is most of the window you came out of. Faintly, from inside, comes the sound of a trowel.
| [flag.death_house_sacrificed] The house is quiet and well-fed. A curtain twitches in an upstairs window, as if to say: come back any time.
| [flag.death_house_children_at_rest] Just a house now, and a sad one. Whatever waited inside it has stopped waiting.
cooldown 10

~ examine:death_house_dead_tree
| A dead tree in the yard, its branches clawing at the upstairs windows. Someone once hung a swing from it; the rope is still there, the seat is not.
cooldown 10

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Blood of the Vine

~ examine:tavern_casks
| Wine casks branded with a wizard's hat and a bunch of grapes. Most ring hollow when you knock; one sloshes, sadly, about a quarter full.
cooldown 10

~ examine:tavern_hearth
| A broad stone hearth, the only warm thing in the village. Someone has carved initials into the mantel: a heart, two names, a date fifty years old.
cooldown 10

~ examine:tavern_stairs
| Stairs to the rooms upstairs. On the bottom step, a sign in Arik's square hand: ROOMS. LOCKS WORK.
cooldown 10

~ examine:tavern_tally_board
| A chalk board of what each regular owes the house. Most columns are short, but one, headed ISMARK, runs to the bottom of the board and carries on along the wall.
cooldown 10

~ examine:aurel_last_note
| A folded sheet of good paper, written in a fast, educated hand. It's addressed to nobody, and signed with two initials.
cooldown 10

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Burgomaster's mansion

~ examine:burgomaster_portrait
| A big, bearded man in a burgomaster's chain, painted glaring at the artist. Someone has hung a black ribbon across the corner of the frame.
cooldown 10

~ examine:kolyan_coffin
| A plain pine coffin, the lid nailed shut. On it lie a sprig of dried flowers, a burgomaster's chain of office and a sword with a notched edge.
| [class:cleric] The coffin is plain and well made. {name} notes no rites have been said; the dead man is waiting for them, the way the dead wait for anything here: badly.
cooldown 10

~ examine:boarded_windows
| The boards are nailed three deep, and the outermost layer is splintered by claws. Light comes through the gaps in thin grey blades.
cooldown 10

~ examine:clawed_front_door
| From inside, the front door is a mess of patches, braces and bent nails. Every repair has a later repair over it.
cooldown 10

~ examine:ireena_sword
| A good sword, well oiled, leaning where a hand can find it without looking. It has been used, recently.
cooldown 10

~ examine:burgomaster_letter
| A letter on the desk, in a big, generous hand that goes small and shaky by the last lines. It was never sent, and never finished.
cooldown 10

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Church and undercroft

~ examine:church_altar_stone
| The altar is a single block of grey stone with a sunburst carved into its face. Someone has scrubbed it so often that the sunburst is wearing away.
| [name:liriel_dawnsong] The sunburst of the Morninglord, worn almost smooth. {name} lays a palm on it the way you take a friend's hand in a sickroom: the stone is cold, and it wasn't always.
cooldown 10

~ examine:morninglord_window
| A round window of colored glass, a rising sun in reds and golds. It's the brightest thing in the church, and it is the color of dusk.
cooldown 10

~ examine:church_pews
| Pews for a hundred, polished smooth by generations. Only the front one is worn recently, in one spot, by one pair of knees.
cooldown 10

~ examine:undercroft_door_gouges
| The doorframe is gouged at knee height, from the floor side, as if something lay down against it and dug. The bar across the door is newer than the frame.
cooldown 10

~ examine:church_register
| The burial register: names, dates and causes in a careful hand. The careful hand gets less careful as the pages go on.
cooldown 10

~ examine:undercroft_niches
| Burial niches along the wall, most of them sealed. Three have been opened from the inside.
cooldown 10

~ examine:undercroft_bones
| Small bones, a great many of them: rats, mostly. They've been cracked open and sucked clean, and then arranged, neatly, by size.
cooldown 10

~ examine:ceiling_marks
| The ceiling is covered in scratches: long scrapes where something crawled, and short ones, in rows of five, where something counted days.
cooldown 10

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Bildrath's Mercantile

~ examine:bildrath_shelves
| Rope coiled to the same diameter, candles in rows of ten, lamp oil with every label facing out. The shelves are fuller than the village has any use for.
cooldown 10

~ examine:last_potion
| A single potion in a locked glass case, red as a cherry and dusty as a tomb. The tag reads 500 GOLD, and the tag is dusty too.
| [class:rogue] A cheap case and a cheaper lock: {name} could have it open before Bildrath finished saying "No". {name} also notices Bildrath noticing.
cooldown 10

~ examine:storeroom_crates
| Crates of stock stacked to the beams, each one stenciled with its contents and its price. One is marked FOR THE BURGOMASTER, PAID, and has never been collected.
cooldown 10

~ examine:bildrath_ledger
| A ledger ruled in red ink, every line squared off with a straightedge. Bildrath has not made a mistake in it in twenty years, and has corrected other people's mistakes in the margins.
cooldown 10

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Mad Mary's house

~ examine:rocking_chair
| The rocking chair has worn two grooves in the floorboards from rocking in the same spot, day and night, for days.
cooldown 10

~ examine:door_locks
| Three locks on the inside of the door, a bolt, a bar and a padlock, all new and all locked the night Gertruda left. None of them was the one that mattered.
cooldown 10

~ examine:cold_stove
| The stove is cold and the pot on it is full of soup that set days ago. Two bowls wait beside it.
cooldown 10

~ examine:gertruda_bed
| A narrow bed, neatly made, with a rag doll propped on the pillow. Under the pillow, when you lift it, is a pressed wildflower of a kind that doesn't grow in town.
cooldown 10

~ examine:gertruda_window
| The window's shutter hangs open on one hinge. The sill is clean, the latch unbroken.
cooldown 10

~ search:gertruda_window
| The latch was lifted from the inside, carefully, so it wouldn't squeak, and her good shoes are gone from under the bed. Nobody carried Gertruda off; she went.

~ examine:gertruda_storybook
| A child's book of tales, read until the spine gave up. One page falls open by itself.
cooldown 10

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Dreams and rests

~ dream:dream_pastry
| {name} dreams of someone lost: a warm kitchen, a familiar voice, a door that opens onto everything that was taken. Waking feels like a theft, and the honey taste won't leave {name}'s mouth.
| [name:godrick_pendlebrook] {name} dreams of Sir Pellam by an inn fire with his boots off, telling the old stories and laughing at the end of every one. Then Pellam picks up a soup ladle, very solemnly, and {name} wakes.
| [name:liriel_dawnsong] {name} dreams of the temple on the hill, the novices singing the sun up, warmth on her face. She wakes to grey Barovian daylight and keeps her eyes shut a while longer.
| [name:thistle] {name} dreams of the hut in the Thornwood: the hounds asleep by the fire, Grandda Fen whittling and saying nothing. She wakes with one hand out, reaching for a hound that isn't there.
| [name:ratatoille] {name} dreams of the inn kitchen at home, flour on every surface, his mother tasting from his spoon and saying nothing, which means perfect. He wakes hungry for something no pastry can fix.
| [name:wren_featherfoot] {name} dreams of Master Sorrel in the practice yard, beckoning him over for one more lesson. Sorrel opens his mouth to begin, and {name} wakes.
| [name:kip_smudgewick] {name} dreams of the orchard in blossom, his daughter Pip laughing in the long grass, his father whistling at the gate. He wakes, and the apricots in his pack smell sweeter than they should.

~ rest:short
| You rest with your backs to a wall that has seen worse. Somewhere a dog barks once and thinks better of it.
| [flag.burgomaster_buried] You rest. The village is a little quieter than it was; or you've grown used to it, which is worse.
cooldown 30

~ rest:long
| You sleep in shifts. Every watch hears wolves, far off, singing to each other about you.
| [flag.ireena_in_party] You sleep in shifts, and whoever has the watch keeps one eye on Ireena's window. Twice in the night something taps on the glass, and nobody answers.
cooldown 60

# --- Hidden finds (docs/story/found_magic_items.md) ---

~ search:barn_beams_stash
| Under the barn's fallen beams, someone hid a javelin wrapped in sacking. Its head is etched with a lightning bolt, and the air around it smells like a coming storm.
once

~ check:perception:barn_beams_stash:failure
| Beams, straw and a smell of old rain. If the barn hides anything, it is under more than you can shift.

~ search:study_panel
| Behind the study desk, a panel lifts away. In the hollow sits a velvet box, and in the box a silver brooch, polished recently and never worn.
once

~ check:investigation:study_panel:failure
| A burgomaster's study: ledgers, complaints and a chair worn to his shape. Nothing more that you can see.

~ search:satchel_lining
| The satchel's lining was slit and sewn shut again. Inside: a pair of crystal lenses in a wire frame, a scholar's best tool and best-kept secret.
once

~ check:investigation:satchel_lining:failure
| Paper, ink and a pen chewed at the end. Whatever else the scholar carried, he took it with him.

~ search:undercroft_priest
| In the oldest niche lies an old priest in rotted vestments. Round his neck, on a chain gone green, hangs a periapt of red stone that is still warm.
once

~ check:perception:undercroft_priest:failure
| The niches go back further than your light does. Someone with sharper eyes might see more.
